Modifications made for wgvim
----------------------------
  In accordance with section 4(b) of the Apache License 2.0, this lists the
  changes. The git history of this repository is the authoritative record.

  * Name and identity: the program, its documentation and its user-facing
    messages are called "wgvim". The executable is "wgvim"; per-user directories
    and environment variables use "wgvim" / "WGVIM" instead of "nvim" / "NVIM".
    Internal identifiers (the nvim_* API functions, the src/nvim/ directory, the
    "vim" Lua namespace) are unchanged so existing Lua plugins keep working.
    Lines that carry credit, copyright, licence or provenance statements were
    deliberately left as written. scripts/rename-wgvim.py records the rename.
  * Dependencies are vendored in deps/ and built offline. Every file is checked
    against the SHA256 recorded in cmake.deps/deps.txt (scripts/verify-deps.sh).
    The build refuses network URLs.
  * The Zig build, the CI configuration and the maintainer scripts that fetch from
    or publish to the network were removed.
  * A tree-sitter parser for C++ (tree-sitter-cpp 0.23.4) was added, with C++ and
    MATLAB highlight queries under runtime/queries/.
  * runtime/spell/en.utf-8.spl is Neovim's English spell file, unchanged: its
    SHA256 (fecabdc949b6a39d32c0899fa2545eab25e63f2ed0a33c4ad1511426384d3070)
    matches neovim/neovim at the snapshot commit. It was loaded and exercised
    (spellbadword, spellsuggest, ]s) under AddressSanitizer/UBSan with no findings.
  * Further changes (removal of network-capable code, security fixes) are listed
    in the git history.

